    "lawCode": "Amd §372, Bank L",
    "lawSection": "Banking Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7973\n\nSPONSOR: MARCHIONE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the banking law, in relation to prohibiting certain\ncheck cashing fees\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 372 of the banking law to provide that a bank\ncannot charge or collect a fee for cashing a check drawn on an account\nthat belongs to the bank, even if the person cashing the check is not a\ncustomer of the bank.\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn a period spanning roughly the last decade, banks have devised various\nfees, of which some are intended by the banks to improve the in-building\nexperience of their own customers. The most notable example of this is\nthe imposition of a fee on non-customers who are cashing checks at a\nbank, even if the check in question is being drawn from an account at\nthat bank. According to the Los Angeles Times in 2017, Bank of America\nis among the most recent of banks to increase their fee on non-customers\nto $8.\n\nIt has been the policy of this State through the banking law to limit,\nwhere possible, excessive fees for taking part in simple financial tran-\nsactions. It does not follow, therefore, that an individual who attempts\nto draw on an account at a bank for which they have a check should be\ncharged a fee for doing so, even if they are not a customer. Not only\ndoes this create an unnecessary financial burden on the person cashing\nthe check, but in some instances it essentially creates a principle of\nimposing two fees on the same account if the person holding the account\nalso pays an annual account fee. This bill would make it so that banking\ninstitutions can no longer impose a non-customer check cashing fee on\nchecks being drawn from an account at that particular bank, thereby\nensuring the State's policy against excessive fees be maintained.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
